WEBVTT

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.709
but maybe you could teach me.

00:04:32.455 --> 00:04:34.716
I mean, you've got to start
somewhere, right?"

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.351
And that was the beginning
of a very strange journey for me.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:41.689
I ended up spending
the better part of the next year

00:04:41.713 --> 00:04:43.507
not only training my memory,

00:04:43.531 --> 00:04:45.467
but also investigating it,

00:04:45.491 --> 00:04:47.475
trying to understand how it works,

00:04:47.499 --> 00:04:49.478
why it sometimes doesn't work,

00:04:49.502 --> 00:04:52.152
and what its potential might be.

00:04:52.176 --> 00:04:54.369
And I met a host
of really interesting people.

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:56.263
This is a guy called E.P.

00:04:56.287 --> 00:04:58.559
He's an amnesic who had, very possibly,

00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:01.268
the worst memory in the world.